  "_comment": "Maps a scanner finding's (source, rule_id) to candidate controls in frameworks/*.json. mapping-agent uses this as a deterministic first pass -- it looks up candidates here, pulls their text from S3, and only asks the LLM to pick/cite/explain among those candidates rather than freely guessing a control_id. Trivy entries are keyed on the id Trivy emits (\"trivy:AWS-0086\"; the tfsec long id aws-s3-block-public-acls it replaced is not in Trivy's report). Entries are grounded in rule_ids actually observed -- first from lambda/iac-scanner/fixtures/vulnerable-sample, then from the third-party repositories in external/ (2026-09-18), then the Kubernetes rules from PugetScope's k8s/ under the pinned scanners (2026-09-19, KSV-*/CKV_K8S_*), then the rules the Kubernetes eval cases raise (2026-09-20); extend as new rule_ids show up in real scans rather than guessing ahead of evidence. A rule with no confident mapping (e.g. pure hygiene checks like missing descriptions) is deliberately left out rather than force-mapped.",
